{
 "id": "wire_release",
 "request": "Outgoing wires arrive by webhook from the payments hub with wire_id, account_id, customer_id, amount, beneficiary_name and beneficiary_country. Write an audit_log row in ops_db at each outcome below (entity 'wire', the wire id, and the action in brackets). Under 10,000: release it [released]. Otherwise payments ops must call the customer back: look up the customer's name and phone in core banking and give PAYMENTS_OPS_EMAIL a task, due in 2 hours, showing the customer's name, phone, the amount and the beneficiary, where they record customer_confirmed (yes, no or unreachable). If nobody has done it in 2 hours, email PAYMENTS_LEAD_EMAIL a reminder and give payments ops the task again, due in 1 hour. If that runs out too, or the customer was unreachable, hold the wire and email the customer that we couldn't reach them [held_no_callback]. If the customer says no, it's fraud: hold the wire, freeze the account and email FRAUD_TEAM_EMAIL [fraud]. If the customer confirms, screen the beneficiary for sanctions. A hit goes to the MLRO (MLRO_EMAIL), due in 4 hours and rejected automatically if nobody decides, who chooses a disposition: false_positive or true_match. A true match, or a rejection: block the wire [blocked], then give the MLRO a second task, due in 1 day, to enter the sar_reference, and record it as the detail of an audit row [sar_filed]. A false positive, or no hit: wires of 1,000,000 or more also need two treasury approvals one after the other (TREASURY_EMAIL, four eyes), then release [released]; a treasury rejection holds the wire [held_by_treasury]. Under 1,000,000: release [released].",
 "apis": [
  "wires.yaml",
  "accounts.yaml",
  "screening.yaml"
 ],
 "tables": {},
 "expect": {
  "trigger": "Webhook",
  "must_have_types": [
   "Approval",
   "Postgres",
   "SendEmail"
  ],
  "must_call": [
   "wires.release",
   "wires.hold",
   "wires.block",
   "accounts.freeze",
   "screening.screen"
  ],
  "max_nodes": 45,
  "min_types": {
   "Approval": 6
  }
 },
 "hidden_tests": [
  {
